{"answerable": true,
"quotes": [
{"source": "S1", "quote": "Any sum of money due and payable to the contractor (including the security deposit returnable to him) under the contract may be withheld or retained by way of lien"},
{"source": "S1", "quote": "in respect of payment of a sum of money arising out of or under any other contract made by the contractor"},
{"source": "S1", "quote": "the contractor shall have no claim for interest or damages whatsoever on this account"},
{"source": "S1", "quote": "in respect of any sum of money withheld or retained under this clause and duly notified as such to the contractor"}
],
"answer": "Yes, the CPWD contract allows this. Money due and payable to the contractor, including the security deposit returnable to it, may be withheld or retained by way of lien [S1]. This can be done against a claim of the Engineer-in-Charge or the Government that arises out of any other contract made by the contractor [S1]. The same clause says the money stays withheld until that claim is either mutually settled or determined by arbitration or by the competent court [S1]. You cannot claim interest on the held-back money. The contractor has no claim for interest or damages on this account, and this covers any sum withheld under the clause and duly notified as such to the contractor [S1]. So the department should notify you that it is withholding the money under this lien [S1].",
"missing": "These are the CPWD contract's terms only. The sources do not say what your own contract or any other agreement provides, or whether the department's claim on the other contract is valid."}

{"answerable": false,
"quotes": [
{"source": "S1", "quote": "Adequate arrangements shall be made for immediate recoupment of the equipment when necessary."},
{"source": "S1", "quote": "The first-aid box shall be kept in charge of a responsible person who shall always be readily available during the working hours of the work place."},
{"source": "S7", "quote": "the arrangements made by the contractor shall be open to inspection by the Labour Officer or Engineer-in-Charge of the department or their representatives."}
],
"answer": "The provided extracts of the Model Rules do not state how often first-aid boxes must be inspected. The first-aid rules cover other points. One box is required for each 150 contract labour or part thereof [S2]. The box must be marked with a red cross on a white background and hold the listed contents [S2]. Used equipment must be recouped immediately when necessary [S1]. The box must be kept in charge of a responsible person who is available during working hours [S1]. The CPWD Safety Code says the contractor's safety arrangements are open to inspection by the Labour Officer or Engineer-in-Charge or their representatives [S7]. That clause gives no frequency and does not mention first-aid boxes specifically.",
"missing": "No periodic inspection interval (daily, weekly, monthly, etc.) for first-aid boxes appears in the provided sources."}
